  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 114 AM MDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nDrier air continues to move into ContDvd region and interior Valleys \nThursday and Friday, with breezy westerly winds likely developing \nspotty critical fire weather conditions across the Central Mtns and \nUpper Arkansas river valley on Thursday, which spreads into portions\nof the San Luis Valley and the middle Arkansas river valley on \nFriday. Otherwise, enough moisture remains in place across the Raton\nMesa and Southern Tier to support chances of storms on Thursday, with\nisolated showers and storms moving back into the ContDvd region \non Friday. Temperatures warm up slightly on Thursday and back to \n5 to 10 degrees above seasonal norms on Friday.  \n\nFor Saturday and into early next week, models continue to indicate\nebbs and flows of available moisture and forcing as occasional waves \ntranslate through the moderate to strong westerly flow aloft across \nthe Northern Tier. This will bring chances of precipitation and \ncooler temperatures with possible fronts across the Plains on Saturday \nand again on Monday. There could be another influx of subtropical \nmoisture across the Desert SW into western Colorado into the middle \nof next week.",
